  - "selective-prediction"
  - "affective-computing"
license: "MIT"
repository-code: "https://github.com/moonlitpayal/sarcasmscope"
abstract: >-
  SARcasmScope is a 3-stage calibrated stacked feature-fusion framework that
  integrates Level-1 sparse WordLex (word 1-2 n-grams with Devanagari/Telugu
  morphological stems, Romanized phonetic keys, and conversational context)
  and CharSub (char 3-5) TF-IDF logistic regression base experts with a
  deterministic linguistic incongruity engine via a 5-fold group-stratified
  out-of-fold MAP Ridge meta-learner, followed by validation temperature scaling
  (T*=0.845) and selective abstention (tau*=0.35). Evaluated once on the frozen
  held-out test split (N=1,123 across 5 public corpora), SARcasmScope improves
  performance from 3.08% to 60.50% recall (67.56% Macro-F1, 68.03% accuracy,
  1.36% Conf-ECE; 80.31% selective accuracy across 45.68% coverage) at 2.856 ms
  P95 (1.632 ms mean) client-side CPU latency.
